  "solution": {
    "text": "Balmer series starts from <math> <mrow> <mtext>n</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow> </math>. So first emission line in atomic spectrum of <math> <mtext>H</mtext> </math> is <math> <mrow> <mtext>2</mtext><mo>→</mo><mtext>3</mtext></mrow> </math><br /><math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mtext>1</mtext> <mtext>λ</mtext> </mfrac> <mtext> </mtext><mtext>=</mtext><mtext> </mtext><msup> <mrow> <mtext>RZ</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msup> <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mtext>1</mtext> <mrow> <msubsup> <mtext>n</mtext> <mtext>1</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msubsup> </mrow> </mfrac> <mfrac> <mrow> <mo>−</mo><mtext>1</mtext></mrow> <mrow> <msubsup> <mtext>n</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msubsup> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </math><br /><math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ν</mi></mrow><mo>-</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>36</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
